Petition to the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine (KMU)

On the creation of a specialized intelligence and support formation “KOZAK” within the Defence Forces of Ukraine for citizens of Ukraine abroad and remote specialists

Text of the petition

Serve where you are. Protect what is yours.

The name KOZAK carries a powerful historical Ukrainian meaning: free warrior, free person, defender.

We, citizens of Ukraine, respectfully address You, the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine, with this petition.

We ask You to consider and adopt the necessary decisions for the creation of a specialized intelligence and support formation under the name KOZAK (KOZAK Intelligence & Support Unit / KOZAK Special Reserve) within the structure of the Defence Forces of Ukraine.

Essence of our proposal

KOZAK is conceived as a closed specialized formation with exclusive assignment of personnel. Its primary objective is to involve citizens of Ukraine who reside permanently or temporarily abroad, as well as specialists capable of performing their duties remotely, in the defence of Ukraine.

Key characteristics of the proposed formation:

- Open primarily to citizens of Ukraine (including persons with dual nationality) who reside outside Ukraine.  
- Exclusive assignment: servicemen serve only within KOZAK and cannot be transferred to other units.  
- Flexibility regarding age, in particular the possibility of serving (especially remotely) after the age of 60 for specialists whose functions do not require physical presence in the combat operations zone.  
- Official military status, documents and legal protection against ordinary mobilisation during the period of validity of the contract or the special period.  
- Emphasis on remote intelligence (OSINT, analysis, languages, networks), cyber support, logistics coordination, fundraising and limited in-person roles when necessary.  
- Possibility of incorporation of friendly foreign citizens under the conditions of existing foreign volunteer contracts.

Why we consider this necessary

Hundreds of thousands of citizens of Ukraine live abroad and possess professional skills, knowledge of languages, analytical capabilities and networks that can strengthen the defence of Ukraine. Many of us are willing to contribute systematically, but currently there is no clear and legally protected pathway that allows serving while remaining abroad and without being subject to ordinary mobilisation into conventional combat units.

The creation of a specialized formation with exclusive assignment and possibilities of remote service will allow:

- mobilising the potential of the diaspora in a structured and controlled manner;  
- providing an official status and documents that protect participants from ordinary mobilisation;  
- strengthening the intelligence, cyber and support capabilities of the Defence Forces;  
- reducing the risk of uncoordinated or informal activity.

Legal basis on which we rely

Our proposal fully complies with the current legislation of Ukraine and develops it:

1. Constitution of Ukraine (Articles 17 and 65) — the defence of Ukraine, the protection of its sovereignty and territorial integrity is the duty of the Ukrainian people and the most important function of the State; the State guarantees the defence capability of Ukraine.

2. Law of Ukraine “On the Defence of Ukraine” No. 1932-XII (in its current wording) — defines the foundations of the defence of Ukraine and the powers of the bodies of state power, in particular of the Cabinet of Ministers, regarding the organisation of defence and the determination of the structure of the Defence Forces.

3. Law of Ukraine “On Military Duty and Military Service” No. 2232-XII (in its current wording), in particular Article 26-1 — provides for voluntary service in the military reserve of the Armed Forces of Ukraine and other military formations on a contractual basis; allows the establishment of particularities of reserve service, including the remote performance of functions by order of the commander.

4. Law of Ukraine “On Mobilisation Preparation and Mobilisation” No. 3543-XII (in its current wording) — regulates mobilisation and the status of persons performing military service or reserve service under contract, creating the legal possibility of protection against ordinary mobilisation for those who already perform specialised service under contract and assignment order.

5. Decree of the President of Ukraine No. 618/2012 “On the Regulation on the Performance of Service by Citizens of Ukraine in the Military Reserve of the Armed Forces of Ukraine” (with subsequent amendments, in particular Decree No. 895/2024) — already establishes the legal mechanism of contractual service in the reserve and the age limits, which may be adjusted for specialised remote roles.

6. Resolutions of the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine regulating the electronic military registration system (Reserve+), in particular Resolution No. 879 of 30 July 2024 and Resolution No. 559 of 16 May 2024 — confirm that the electronic military registration document has full legal force and, together with the contract and the assignment order, constitutes the proper confirmation of status.

7. Existing legal basis for the service of foreigners under contract in the Armed Forces of Ukraine (Decree of the President No. 248/2016 and subsequent acts) — already allows the incorporation of friendly foreign volunteers on a contractual basis.

8. Current legislative and organisational work relating to the creation of the Cyber Forces of the Armed Forces of Ukraine and the development of remote cyber-reserve mechanisms — demonstrates that specialised remote formations are already recognised as necessary and possible within the framework of current policy.

Proposed path of implementation that we ask You to support

1. Immediate launch of a registered Ukrainian military charity/foundation as the initial public and coordination instrument (fully possible under current legislation on charitable organisations and support to the army).  
2. Simultaneous preparation by You of the legal basis for the official creation of the KOZAK unit by decree of the President, resolution of the Cabinet of Ministers or order of the Ministry of Defence, using the existing mechanisms of contractual service, foreign volunteers and remote cyber-reserve service.  
3. Transition of the verified specialists from the foundation to official contractual service under KOZAK orders once the unit is created.  
4. Authorisation of remote service by order of the commander (already practised in accordance with the current rules of the cyber reserve).  
5. Use of the electronic military registration document (Reserve+) together with the contract and the assignment order as legal protection against ordinary mobilisation.

Funding model

- Official monetary remuneration in accordance with the standards of the Defence Forces (base salary + rank + length of service + supplements for special tasks), as provided for in the current legislation on the monetary remuneration of servicemen.  
- Additional support through a transparent foundation mechanism (including possible citizen contributions recorded in an audited register), which are converted into additional stipends or unit resources in accordance with the legislation of Ukraine on charitable activity and support to defence.

Slogan and identity

“Serve where you are. Protect what is yours.”

The name KOZAK carries a powerful historical Ukrainian meaning — free warrior, free person, defender — and is suitable for international branding and possible adaptation by other national communities.

Our official request to You

We, the Ukrainian people, ask You, the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine, to instruct the corresponding ministries (in the first place the Ministry of Defence and the Ministry of Justice) to study this proposal thoroughly, prepare the necessary legal and organisational basis and adopt the decision on the creation of the specialised formation KOZAK within the Defence Forces of Ukraine.

The creation of such a unit will allow Ukraine to involve its citizens abroad more effectively in the defence of the State, providing them with a clear legal status, protection and a meaningful form of service that fully complies with the Constitution and the laws of Ukraine.

We trust that You will give this matter the due attention in the interest of the defence capability of Ukraine and the unity of the Ukrainian people.
